The Pillars game (src/main/java/me/petr1furious/potatominigames/games/pillars/
and src/main/resources/games/pillars.yml) is a Java rewrite of PillarPeril's
Kotlin code, written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) and modified: it runs
on the Potato Minigames framework and its slime-world arenas, and drops
PillarPeril's translations, metrics, update checker, command hooks, block
rollback and game modifiers. Each file derived from PillarPeril says so at its top.

This fork contains downstream modifications maintained by tiom4eg (2026):
queue voting, spectator cameras, solo test games, Warfare map rotation,
Bingo lockout, Pillars modes and events, player-owned Pillars presets,
and world lifecycle and gadget fixes.

